CAT(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    cat - concatenate files and display text

SYNOPSIS
    cat [-nbsA] [file...]

DESCRIPTION
    Copies files to stdout, or stdin when no file is given. - names stdin.
    -n numbers all lines, -b numbers nonempty lines and overrides -n,
    -s squeezes repeated empty lines, -A displays control characters,
    tabs as ^I and line endings as $. Numbering spans all input files.

SEE ALSO
    sh(1), man(1), index(7)
